s://scontent-iad3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t39.30808-1/466068478_10169675685920058_754274707041890859_n.jpg?stp=cp0_dst-jpg_tt6&cstp=mx960x960&ctp=s32x32&_nc_cat=110&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=e99d92&_nc_ohc=Upji3JORPEIQ7kNvwHVljLh&_nc_oc=AdqgGm4InJJQlGINhNmmlz200nxwaLsah4hE52O-_4ratix3BKDppwJSyNga1PIrQ9Q&_nc_zt=24&_nc_ht=scontent-iad3-1.xx&_nc_gid=RZ0m62h4dhnkRmBHLxh75g&_nc_ss=78180&oh=00_AQQSt1QgUxJfxBZndRchKZtzHq9U_3VmzAkjWG5Oidk2oA&oe=6AF3DBA1\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"744275328\",\n          \"name\": \"Monica Romero Matthews\",\n          \"url\": \"https://www.facebook.com/Monica.Romero.Matthews\",\n          \"profilePictureUrl\": \"https://scontent-iad3-2.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t39.30808-1/468745726_10164792738440329_6758959915352880099_n.jpg?stp=cp0_dst-jpg_tt6&cstp=mx1092x1092&ctp=s32x32&_nc_cat=111&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=1d2534&_nc_ohc=RFE9Mra1dvsQ7kNvwE6Scrk&_nc_oc=Adpt7AFmbMwhQkHCpBIcd3sQIY61iT2YlUTr3ACxus55J-CZbYsogmKDzbHhrFZLyzU&_nc_zt=24&_nc_ht=scontent-iad3-2.xx&_nc_gid=RZ0m62h4dhnkRmBHLxh75g&_nc_ss=78180&oh=00_AQRwIPpS2D8UJuusY4Vs6TCa6Hnic2-WbD2KtwnCjmNIlw&oe=6AF3D05C\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"pfbid034yrsCkwJLyZ6eAsdYcvnZMkw8ZqPEKFPCYQsgYfW2ERXSgSkKsb7YYJnDpzpqNE3l\",\n          \"name\": \"Kelly Johnson Gyselman\",\n          \"url\": null,\n          \"profilePictureUrl\": \"https://scontent-iad6-1.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t39.30808-1/624647513_10162334155956705_8140047733235309659_n.jpg?stp=cp0_dst-jpg_tt6&cstp=mx853x853&ctp=s32x32&_nc_cat=100&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=e99d92&_nc_ohc=QXBcgZZvf8UQ7kNvwGEX2I7&_nc_oc=AdqC7l1fgY3JG235PKmyQ5G0CGFtEhoiJOxpo1KXmIJlutFPdtV913ZUGfPmhsCrd9M&_nc_zt=24&_nc_ht=scontent-iad6-1.xx&_nc_gid=RZ0m62h4dhnkRmBHLxh75g&_nc_ss=78180&oh=00_AQTWuXXVDDw2sWugBdWZRisWD8QHekqfg5DaDQCvDIUTaQ&oe=6AF3EBC3\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"42109726\",\n          \"name\": \"Jon Richards\",\n          \"url\": \"https://www.facebook.com/ACTSATtutor\",\n          \"profilePictureUrl\": \"https://scontent-iad6-1.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t39.30808-1/480273513_10105672819416632_7939098330073237405_n.jpg?stp=cp0_dst-jpg_tt6&cstp=mx753x753&ctp=s32x32&_nc_cat=107&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=1d2534&_nc_ohc=lxRp-f1xnw8Q7kNvwGypKMM&_nc_oc=AdqNdV3cmnSLhqtngys0HRE40GIyXlAoNCrwqoVb6qFV_tKi8zfHEKfQDYcNrzjDhOQ&_nc_zt=24&_nc_ht=scontent-iad6-1.xx&_nc_gid=RZ0m62h4dhnkRmBHLxh75g&_nc_ss=78180&oh=00_AQSz75n4U7emA5ic1xad1tTZUzqEzSiZku_qJkb5uW8v4Q&oe=6AF3DC89\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"pfbid02xDaUAmvqeF7JQQm9U54cBhrKdkdxY1tbeofpHCXY9wdS5o1pKUbEF5hCTZZP1mpGl\",\n          \"name\": \"Robert Farrington\",\n          \"url\": null,\n          \"profilePictureUrl\": \"https://scontent-iad3-2.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t39.30808-1/468960917_10110620786415714_6824800720061421642_n.jpg?stp=cp0_dst-jpg_tt6&cstp=mx1194x1194&ctp=s32x32&_nc_cat=105&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=e99d92&_nc_ohc=oJikkhhUVw4Q7kNvwEFDIah&_nc_oc=AdqvSX_tasYuTqEaqqWNsYCbRfm27Ys8pqCGS27x3CJkl-1KNwRF7Ak7VZDDiqXjMXE&_nc_zt=24&_nc_ht=scontent-iad3-2.xx&_nc_gid=RZ0m62h4dhnkRmBHLxh75g&_nc_ss=78180&oh=00_AQRTXUWgRJRXJrytYuKD2fB0NlZ8zyTvrdi6dfZoJlShYg&oe=6AF3D599\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"activity\": {\n        \"postsLastDay\": 15,\n        \"postsLastMonth\": 543,\n        \"newMembersText\": \"No new members in the last week\"\n      },\n      \"rules\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"1704256026979306\",\n          \"title\": \"No Self-Promotion, Spam, or External Websites:\",\n          \"description\": \"Self-promotion, solicitation, spam, or reshared content is not allowed in this group. Members may not post links—including those promoting businesses, services, products, other Facebook groups, or external websites. I may occasionally share affiliate links and earn a small commission at no extra cost to you; this helps support the group. To be considered as an approved partner or expert, email Dormroomsandbeyond@gmail.com with your info. – Tamara\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"1704256113645964\",\n          \"title\": \"Respect Each Other & the Group\",\n          \"description\": \"Treat all members with respect—healthy debate is fine, but kindness is required. This is a supportive space for parents to share experiences and offer constructive advice. Posts or comments that are rude, offensive, or inappropriate will be removed. This group also relies on mutual trust: what’s shared here should stay here, as discussions may be sensitive or personal.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"1704256180312624\",\n          \"title\": \"Limit DuplicateQuestions\",\n          \"description\": \"We often get the same questions (like FAFSA, Common App, and other common subjects) multiple times a day. To keep the group easy to follow, please use the search bar or check recent posts before posting. If you don’t find what you need, you’re welcome to ask again another day.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"2030033517734887\",\n          \"title\": \"Topic-Specific Posts & Days\",\n          \"description\": \"To keep the group organized and easy to navigate, we’ve created dedicated posts and themed days for popular topics such as Senior Sundays, school-specific admission threads, homecoming, and prom. If your post fits one of these categories, it may be declined and you’ll be directed to the appropriate thread. This helps reduce repetition and ensures everyone can quickly find what they’re looking for\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"1876900956381478\",\n          \"title\": \"This is a Nationwide Group\",\n          \"description\": \"This is a nationwide group. Please refrain from asking questions specific to a particular high school. If you have questions that pertain to your specific high school, we recommend finding and joining your school's dedicated Facebook group\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"1715036555901253\",\n          \"title\": \"Stay On Topic:\",\n          \"description\": \"Please keep posts and comments relevant to the interests and concerns of parents of the Class of 2026. Off-topic posts may be removed.  No Political or Religious Discussions: To maintain a neutral and supportive environment, discussions involving politics or religion are not permitted.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"1715036562567919\",\n          \"title\": \"Report Issues to Admins:\",\n          \"description\": \"If you see something that violates these rules or seems inappropriate, please report it to the admins. Do not engage in public arguments or confrontations.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"requestId\": \"req_30411147-3f75-44f3-b44e-2db1f4238116\",\n    \"creditsCharged\": 1,\n    \"version\": \"v1\"\n  }\n}"},{"type":"text","text":"{\"conversation_id\":\"01a1b1a8-f3da-7133-888d-53ab45643056\"}"}],"structuredContent":{"data":{"lookupStatus":"found","group":{"platform":"facebook","id":"1688114615260114","url":"https://www.facebook.com/groups/1688114615260114","name":"Parents of Class of 2026-Parenting Beyond The Nest","description":"Welcome to Parents of Class of 2026 – PARENTING BEYOND THE NEST, a community for parents whose students have graduated and are beginning their next chapter. Whether that journey includes college, the military, trade school, a gap year, or entering the workforce, this is a place to navigate it together.\n\nGraduation may mark the end of high school, but it isn't the end of parenting. Whether you're adjusting to an empty nest, helping your student settle into college, or still juggling younger children at home, this community is here to support you through this new season of life.\n\nThis group is a place to:\n🔴 Share encouragement as we adjust to our evolving roles as parents\n🟡 Exchange advice, experiences, and lessons learned along the way\n🟢 Find support and community with parents navigating the same transition\n\nOur students may be launching into adulthood, but here we focus on what it means to continue PARENTING BEYOND THE NEST. We're so glad you're here.\n\nWe have a great group of experts and seasoned parents who are here to answer questions, offer support, and share valuable insights every step of the way.\n\nNote: This group is part of the Ready Set College network of parent communities, including Parents of the Classes of 2025,2026, 2027, 2028, 2029, 2030, 2031, 2032, and beyond.\n\nDisclaimer: Some posts shared by admin may contain affiliate links. I may earn a small commission at zero cost to members. Your support helps cover the time and expense of providing free resources, content, and support for this community. We appreciate your support!\n\nAbout Ready Set College\nHi! I'm Tamara, founder of Ready Set College. I'm not a large company or corporation, just a mom of two who has experienced the college journey firsthand. One of my children has already graduated from college and grad school, and the other is currently in college, so I've experienced many of the same questions, challenges, and milestones you're facing now. My goal is to create a supportive community where parents can connect, learn, and help one another through every stage of the journey. If you're interested in partnering with our community, you can reach me at dormroomsandbeyond@gmail.com","createdAt":"2024-04-26T15:41:24.000Z","historySummary":"Group created on April 26, 2024. Name last changed on August 19, 2026.","privacy":{"label":"Public","description":"Anyone can see who's in the group and what they post."},"visibility":{"label":"Visible","description":"Anyone can find this group."},"categories":[{"id":"1282128838821054","name":"Education"},{"id":"354007908454271","name":"College & Adult Education"}],"memberCount":223699,"administratorCount":4,"moderatorCount":10,"administrators":[{"id":"61570130213944","name":"Dorm Rooms Of Mississippi","url":"https://www.facebook.com/dorm.rooms.of.mississippi","profilePictureUrl":"https://scontent-iad3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t39.30808-1/732179035_122164639382671007_5508250522460523010_n.jpg?stp=cp0_dst-jpg_tt6&cstp=mx1254x1254&